            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass in the &quot;megaobese&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>707-9; discussion 710</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="HYPOTHESIS" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass is a safe and effective procedure in patients with a body mass index (BMI; calculated as weight in kilograms divided by the square of height in meters) of 70 or greater.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">A retrospective analysis of patients with a BMI of 70 or greater who underwent laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass by a single surgeon.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">A university-affiliated community hospital in Allentown, Pa.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A nonconsecutive series of 9 patients with a BMI of 70 or greater who met traditional criteria for a bariatric procedure.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Laparoscopic approach to Roux-en-Y gastric bypass with stapled anastomoses.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Patient medical records were reviewed for length of stay, complications, operative time, comorbidities, and weight loss. Seven patients were women and 2 were men. Comorbidities included dyspnea on exertion, peripheral edema, arthritis, sleep apnea, hypertension, diabetes mellitus, asthma, hypothyroidism, gastroesophageal reflux disease, peptic ulcer disease, and heart disease. Eight of 9 procedures were successfully completed laparoscopically. One patient was converted to an open procedure. One patient developed a marginal ulcer postoperatively. No other complications occurred. Operative time ranged from 122 to 330 minutes (mean, 203 minutes). Length of stay averaged 1.2 days. Overall weight loss was 49% of excess body weight at 1 year after surgery.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass is safe and effective in patients with a BMI of 70 or greater.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
